															</div>
				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/stormbreath" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(3075960); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=3075960&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1606985040" alt="stormbreath" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=3075960)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/stormbreath" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(3075960); return false;" >stormbreath</a></span> <span class="odate time_1529635754 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">22 Jun 2018 02:49</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-3845451">
									

<p>Somewhat recently, somebody on reddit <a href="https://www.reddit.com/r/SCP/comments/8e956p/theres_a_lot_of_scps_that_are_swords_are_there/">asked if there were any shield SCPs</a>. The answer was &quot;No, I guess there aren't?&quot;<sup class="footnoteref"><a id="footnoteref-150383-1" href="javascript:;" class="footnoteref" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.utils.scrollToReference('footnote-150383-1')">1</a></sup> Feeling that was a weird gap in the site, I decided to write one. At the same time, I was somewhat annoyed by the historical items onsite, which tended to just pop up and not actually have any indepth history. I decided to combine the concepts, and write a shield with a detailed provenance.</p>
<p>Anyway, I started this in April and finished it a couple days ago. Then the 4k Contest was announced as history. This was <em>never</em> intended to be a 4000, and while I could turn the very basic skeleton (of an extensive provance) into a 4k entry, I had completely coated that skeleton in non-4k material. So I made the decision to post this ahead of the contest.</p>
<p>There should be enough info in this to figure out where the shield was from 1096-1104.</p>
<p>Thanks to Modern_Erasmus, ihp, zzuxon, NineVolt, drblackbox, razzy, subtletea, and DrChandra for looking this over, and Tufto for giving me the name Esma'il Kashani.</p>
<p><strong>ATTRIBUTION:</strong> Image is sourced from <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bronze_sheild,_1200-700_BC_British_Museum.jpg">here</a> with minor edits by myself. Licensed under the Creative Commons Attribution-Share Alike 2.0 Generic.</p>
<div class="footnotes-footer">
<div class="title">Footnotes</div>
<div class="footnote-footer" id="footnote-150383-1"><a href="javascript:;" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.utils.scrollToReference('footnoteref-150383-1')">1</a>. I have since confirmed that this is the case - this is the only shield SCP on the wiki.</div>
</div>

