			<div class="content" id="post-content-3856957">
									

<p>Dry as all hell but something I do appreciate for world-building.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>To demonstrate the anomalous properties of SCP-3668, a secondary agent is to wield SCP-3668 while the leading agent repeatedly fires a handgun at the secondary agent's head.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>This immediately broke immersion for me. I can't for the life of me imagine why SCPF personnel would not only be allowed to carry a loaded firearm in the presence of POTUS, but actually be encouraged to draw and fire it? I gave this the benefit of the doubt, but in reading the description, it's pretty clear that something this drastic isn't really all that necessary, and having this touted at the end as something low-risk reinforced the notion that it's an all-around terrible inclusion in an otherwise solid piece.</p>
<p>It may sound cool and interesting, it may be an attempt at a hook, but sometimes narrative should take a backseat to verisimilitude.</p>

